<title>BRAZIL: Brazil exports $3.789 bln in December.</title>
<headline>Brazil exports $3.789 bln in December.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil exported $3.789 billion in goods in the month of December, with a daily average of $189.5 million, the Ministry of Industry and Commerce said.</p>
<p>The Ministry said in a statement that total exports in 1996 were $47.746 billion, up from $46.506 billion in 1995, or an increase of 2.67 percent.  </p>
<p>Daily average exports in 1996 were $191 million, versus $186.8 million the year before, the Ministry said.</p>
<p>((-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom, 5561 223-0358))</p>
